From 506ee2e879b8cebfe241c718cf4536d134f60b23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:16:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): read session context without durable write
 receipts [daveey]

Why: real dispatched Kanban whole-boot trace run18579 spends ~0.67s in
get_session through compression.context. Read observations currently queue
and acknowledge a durable journal entry and write an owner receipt carrying
the session snapshot. This creates fsync and SQLite write work for a fresh
observation and permits immutable replay of what should be current context.

Add authenticated worker.sessionContext on the existing owner transport.
Verify live producer/adoption, current serving epoch, execution generation,
status and readable lineage; assignment and context use one read snapshot.
Serialize worker reads behind acknowledged writes and reject pending or failed
journals. Preserve bounded transport retries as fresh reads, never write
fallback. Only explicit JSON-RPC -32601 negotiates the old receipt path for
rolling upgrades. No worker process, claim, pid/birth or durable-write fences
change. No new config or preload policy.

Proof: new query suite RED (23 failed,6 passed) on base then GREEN. 47 direct
store/RPC consumer files pass 751 tests; authority/contract/generator suites
also pass. Ten anchored mutants killed (pending/failure ordering, downgrade,
retry, owner epoch/status, read snapshot, wire error code). scripts/check:
21 checks OK on staged change. Real deployed >=50-session latency acceptance
remains outstanding; do not interpret these as whole-boot latency results.

Warm pool not built: real trace has no meaningful allowed SDK-only share;
previous audited prototype gain0.127s/62MB could not justify its bootstrap
fidelity risks. No run_agent/model_tools/plugin/MCP/config preloading.
